      "reviewer": "Claude Opus 5",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-25T07:50:00Z",
      "note": "The anchor transaction is the whole exploit: GovernorAlpha.execute(11) sets the fFTS collateral factor to 0.7, Chain.submit() is then called directly by the attacker contract with four forged signature triples and sets FTS/USD to 4e34, and thirteen Fortress markets are borrowed out in the same transaction. The four addresses ecrecover returns from the submitted signatures all hold zero balance of the validator stake token 0x648f235ec0c24fe170bd0822d2fef442880a25ee, and submit() still writes the values, which is the defect. The attacker sent no other successful transaction against Fortress; the following transaction 0x851a65865e is withdrawAll() moving proceeds out of the attacker contract. The Chain feed is not upgradeable: its runtime code hash is identical at the deployment block 13441159 and at block 17634662 and its EIP-1967 implementation slot is zero, so the exploited code is 146.3 days old, deployed by 0xa6e4ffa19b213abea258ae72e8e1a209b9e543e7, which is unrelated to the attacker. Loss is the exploit contract net token delta plus its BNB balance change, valued at DefiLlama prices for the incident timestamp. The governance proposal that made fFTS collateral was a necessary precondition but carried no value on its own: the 5,000 fFTS minted from 100 FTS only supported the borrows once the fabricated price applied."
    }
  ],
